[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2914985740","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106884#issuecomment-2914985740","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106884","id":2914985740,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tvycM","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T05:29:39Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T05:29:39Z","body":"We probably should stop making official builds for these archs first, and see the reaction. But it's likely too late in 4.5 dev cycle even for this.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2914985740/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2915055109","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106884#issuecomment-2915055109","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106884","id":2915055109,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6twDYF","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T06:05:59Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T15:16:28Z","body":"While I'm in favor of stopping distributing 32-bit builds eventually[^1], I don't see why we should drop support for compiling for 32-bit x86 and arm platforms.\r\n\r\nIt's not a lot of code nor much maintenance burden, and Godot aims to be as portable as possible and compatible with lower end devices, some of which are 32-bit.\r\n\r\nUnlike ppc32 removed in #106390 which was a purely theoretical build target that very likely can't *run* Godot, arm32 and x86 platforms can run Godot fine.\r\n\r\nAnd indeed, wasm32 is here to stay and there's no guarantee that wasm64 will ever be the preferred option for web (especially given its bigger binary size, which is a big issue for web games).\r\n\r\n[^1]: I would start first with dropping official binaries for the editor, but keep 32-bit export templates, so users who want to can still support those architectures with their games.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2915055109/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916284990","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106884#issuecomment-2916284990","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106884","id":2916284990,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t0vo-","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T13:12:18Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T13:12:18Z","body":"Ahhhh, I misunderstood the internal discussions regarding 32-bit in that case. It's indeed fairly low-maintenance to keep `x86_32` and `arm32`, and that is consistent with the promise of low-end support, so this isn't nearly as pertinent as I imagined\r\n\r\nClosing, as this doesn't solve a problem that actually exists","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916284990/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916458003","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106884#issuecomment-2916458003","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106884","id":2916458003,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t1Z4T","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T13:56:24Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T13:56:24Z","body":"> Doing so will also free up space in the build matrix, so that official builds can be made faster and the export templates TPZ will be smaller. This extra space could in turn be reused to provide faster builds catering to modern CPUs (AVX2), while #59595 would be used to \"upgrade\" the current x86_64 binaries as the baseline. (There's still the challenge of providing some kind of automatic detection at startup though, e.g. using a launcher script that is generated on export to launch the correct binary.)\r\n\r\nIf this is a concern, we could always make 32-bit more \"second class\", by just removing them from the build matrix (and / or not provide official builds). We don't need to drop support _entirely_ for this.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916458003/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916727214","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106884#issuecomment-2916727214","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106884","id":2916727214,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t2bmu","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T15:16:06Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T15:18:04Z","body":"> > Doing so will also free up space in the build matrix, so that official builds can be made faster and the export templates TPZ will be smaller. This extra space could in turn be reused to provide faster builds catering to modern CPUs (AVX2), while #59595 would be used to \"upgrade\" the current x86_64 binaries as the baseline. (There's still the challenge of providing some kind of automatic detection at startup though, e.g. using a launcher script that is generated on export to launch the correct binary.)\r\n> \r\n> If this is a concern, we could always make 32-bit more \"second class\", by just removing them from the build matrix (and / or not provide official builds). We don't need to drop support _entirely_ for this.\r\n\r\nYeah I also think we could make some less-frequently needed platforms opt-in, namely:\r\n- Linux x86_32, armv7, and arm64[^1]\r\n- Windows x86_32 and arm64[^1]\r\n- Android x86_32 and armv7\r\n\r\nIdeally, we'd have a system to download export templates individually instead of 1GB tpz, and just have the default config to download the \"first class\" platforms, with the options to add-in support for other architectures when needed.\r\n\r\n[^1]: arm64 usage is likely going to grow, but for now it's still niche and not something that most users target yet. For example Steam doesn't support arm64 Linux and Windows yet.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916727214/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]